# Admin auth — agent reference

Applies whenever a change touches the `/bookings` routes, the new admin-only edge functions, or guest-form dev toggles (`?dev=true`, non-production builds).

## 1. Auth model

- Provider: **Supabase Auth** with **Google OAuth**.
- Client: `@supabase/supabase-js` (add to `ui/package.json` when implementing).
- Single shared Supabase client: `ui/src/lib/supabase/client.ts`.
- Entry point: **`/for-hosts/login`** — calls `supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth({ provider: 'google' })`. Legacy **`/sign-in`** redirects here.

## 2. Allow list

- Only these emails may access admin routes and admin edge functions:
  - **Config**: `ADMIN_ALLOWED_EMAILS` — comma-separated env var in `supabase/.env.local` and Supabase dashboard.
  - **Default value**: `kamehome.azurenorth@gmail.com`.
- The allow list is enforced **server-side** on every admin edge function via `_shared/auth.ts#verifyAdminJwt(req)`. Never trust the client.
- Client also reads `ADMIN_ALLOWED_EMAILS` (via `VITE_ADMIN_ALLOWED_EMAILS`) for an immediate UX reject, but never as the only gate.

## 3. Route guards (UI)

- New component: `ui/src/features/dashboard/bookings/components/RequireAdmin.tsx`.
  - Shows a loader while the session hydrates.
  - Redirects to **`/for-hosts/login`** (via `hostLoginPath`) if unauthenticated.
  - Shows a generic "access restricted" message if the signed-in email is not allow-listed (no disclosure of which emails are allowed; signs the user out from that view).
- Applied to: `/bookings`, `/bookings/:bookingId`, `/finance`, `/maintenance`, `/notifications`, `/settings`, and any other admin route added later.
- The existing public routes (`/`, `/form`, `/success`, `/calendar`) stay unauthenticated.

## 4. Guest form dev controls (`GuestForm.tsx`)

- **Production (`VITE_NODE_ENV === 'production'`):** no dev checkbox panel; submits use full save + storage + calendar + sheet flags as wired in `submit-form`, and **New Booking Request** email runs by default (`sendEmail` omitted → treated as on server-side).
- **Non-production:** dev panel shows save/storage/calendar/sheet/**Send email** toggles (**all on by default**; uncheck to skip). **`sendEmail=false`** skips the owner notify only.
- **`?dev=true`** on `/form` enables the same panel in production builds when operators need to flip individual API flags (rare).

There is **no** separate test-booking mode, `?testing=true`, `is_test_booking` column, or test-data cleanup edge function — use local/staging projects instead.

## 5. Dev controls panel (admin detail page)

Shown on `/bookings/:bookingId`. Checkbox list driving what happens on the next action click:

| Checkbox                          | Shown when                              | Replaces the old                                                  |
| --------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Save to database                  | always                                  | `saveToDatabase`                                                  |
| Save images to storage            | always                                  | `saveImagesToStorage`                                             |
| Generate GAF / pet request PDFs   | only from `PENDING_REVIEW`              | `generatePdf` (was guest-form query param; now transition-only)   |
| **Send GAF request email**        | only from `PENDING_REVIEW`              | renamed from `Send email notification`                            |
| **Send Parking broadcast email**  | only when `need_parking`                | new                                                               |
| **Send Pet request email**        | only when `has_pets`                    | new                                                               |
| **Send Acknowledgement email**    | only from `PENDING_REVIEW`              | renamed / split from legacy                                       |
| **Send Ready-for-check-in email** | only from GAF / parking / pet stages    | gates server + UI                                                 |
| **Send SD refund form email**     | only when status is `READY_FOR_CHECKIN` | email guest `/sd-form` link on transition to `READY_FOR_CHECKOUT` |
| Update Google Calendar            | always                                  | `updateGoogleCalendar`                                            |
| Update Google Sheets              | always                                  | `updateGoogleSheets`                                              |

All checkboxes start **checked** so the next action runs the full happy path (DB + Calendar + Sheet + the emails that apply to that transition). Admins **uncheck** the specific side effects they want to skip for that run. In production they are authoritative — flipping a checkbox off means "really don't do it". The server's `flag()` helper in `_shared/workflowOrchestrator.ts` treats `undefined` as `true`, so this UI default mirrors the server default.

## 6. Server contract

- All admin edge functions (`list-bookings`, `transition-booking`, `sync-booking-integrations`, `upload-booking-asset`, `send-sd-refund-form-email`, `parking-broadcast-email`, `cancel-booking`, …) set **`verify_jwt = false`** in `supabase/config.toml` **and** must call `verifyAdminJwt(req)` as the first line of the handler.
  - **Why `false` in config.toml:** Kong's `verify_jwt = true` gate uses the legacy HS256 JWT secret and rejects newer ES256 auth tokens issued by Supabase local dev (≥ 1.x). Our `verifyAdminJwt` calls `supabase.auth.getUser(jwt)` which handles both algorithms correctly **and** also enforces the `ADMIN_ALLOWED_EMAILS` allow-list — making it a strictly stronger gate than Kong's check.
  - **The function body check IS the security boundary** — never skip `verifyAdminJwt(req)` on the assumption that Kong already validated the token.
- The public functions (`submit-form`, `get-form`, `get-booked-dates`, `get-guest-payment-info`, `get-sd-form`, `submit-sd-form`) keep `verify_jwt = false` — guests must still be able to hit them with only the anon key.

## 7. Env vars summary (new)

| Var                                    | Scope | Purpose                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |
| -------------------------------------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `ADMIN_ALLOWED_EMAILS`                 | edge  | Comma-separated allow list (server-enforced).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |
| `VITE_ADMIN_ALLOWED_EMAILS`            | UI    | UX reject only; never the only gate.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
| `PARKING_OWNER_EMAILS`                 | edge  | _(Removed — use **`app_settings.parking_owner_emails`** per property.)                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
| `GMAIL_API_WEB_CLIENT_JSON`            | edge  | Web OAuth client JSON for **Connect Google** on **`/settings`** (Gmail + Calendar + Sheets scopes); redirect URI `{SUPABASE_URL}/functions/v1/google-mail-oauth-callback`. Pair with `GMAIL_OAUTH_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY`. Enable Calendar + Sheets APIs and scopes on the OAuth consent screen. |
| `GMAIL_OAUTH_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY`     | edge  | 32-byte AES key (64 hex or base64) for encrypting Gmail refresh tokens + Telegram bot tokens in DB.                                                                                                                                                                                            |
| `GMAIL_OAUTH_ALLOWED_RETURN_ORIGINS`   | edge  | Comma-separated SPA origins allowed by `google-mail-oauth-start` (defaults include local Vite).                                                                                                                                                                                                |
| `SD_REFUND_CRON_EMAIL_LEAD_MINUTES`    | edge  | _(Removed — use **`app_settings.sd_refund_cron_email_lead_minutes`** per property.)                                                                                                                                                                                                            |
| `SD_REFUND_CRON_MAX_CHECKOUT_AGE_DAYS` | edge  | _(Removed — use **`app_settings.sd_refund_cron_max_checkout_age_days`** per property.)                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
| `TELEGRAM_*_CRON_SECRET`               | edge  | _(Optional)_ Cron auth headers only (`TELEGRAM_CRON_SECRET`, `TELEGRAM_STAFF_CRON_SECRET`, `TELEGRAM_ADMIN_CRON_SECRET`, `TELEGRAM_FINANCE_CRON_SECRET`, `TELEGRAM_MAINTENANCE_CRON_SECRET`). Bot tokens + chat IDs are **per-property DB** (`telegram_*_settings`), not env.                  |
| `GEMINI_API_KEYS`                      | edge  | _(Optional)_ Comma-separated Gemini API keys from **different** Google Cloud projects; round-robin with 429 failover. Falls back to `GEMINI_API_KEY` if unset.                                                                                                                                 |
| `GEMINI_API_KEY`                       | edge  | _(Optional, legacy)_ Single Gemini key. Used only when `GEMINI_API_KEYS` is not set.                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
| `GROQ_API_KEY`                         | edge  | _(Optional)_ Groq free-tier key (Llama 4 Scout vision). Fallback when all Gemini keys are rate-limited. Sign up at `https://console.groq.com`.                                                                                                                                                 |
| `TELEGRAM_FINANCE_CRON_SECRET`         | edge  | _(Optional)_ When set, `telegram-finance-cron` requires header `X-Telegram-Cron-Secret` with the same value.                                                                                                                                                                                   |
| `TELEGRAM_MAINTENANCE_CRON_SECRET`     | edge  | _(Optional)_ When set, `telegram-maintenance-cron` requires header `X-Telegram-Cron-Secret` with the same value.                                                                                                                                                                               |

Remember to update `docs/PROJECT.md` §11 Environment variables in the same commit that introduces any of these.

## 8. Don'ts

- Don't pass JWTs or admin emails through URL query strings.
- Don't add a second Supabase client — share `ui/src/lib/supabase/client.ts`.
- Don't hardcode `kamehome.azurenorth@gmail.com` in code; read from env.
- Don't build admin features that work without `verifyAdminJwt` server-side — the allow list is the one real gate.
